{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0bd0f5f22d71c11d5ef518b271eb0f8eae03cad958f334c27546cd479d10c770","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8665a3543ee3686f79b62c5c968c894530a82896dbc0c3a480e72aa99eedd88a"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"The package can be imported as a library; the core reportedly has no dependency on the CLI/TUI layers, letting users build their own interface on top.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_13bd75b62e6872704931e609b0d874af568111c79315a5b02ed41b89bb2279eb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a08147c86024f8ab00f1c174724ef22e37ec25f455fd75a43f2f2347aaaa6eb2","slc_d110dd63edb5e77ae4120c6c5b1900d5cd43eac4694381477ef9e3350ef5f593"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"A CTO-style agent decomposes a high-level goal into tasks and delegates them; failed tasks auto-retry with exponential backoff and stalled agents are killed and re-queued by zombie detection.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4fca750d1579bb89b05b5efa0f3a5c80935ae5805b75527c1a6f1887e4112fe6","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f4ea60b0d9455be0edcb9e755cd6cfe5e7133410d29d278a94b5263167bd9521","slc_f819496f3b72405e8a191593cc5c9a1ef58ed1ad27a8e11208708ec79a043f2a"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"Storage is file-based using YAML/JSON/JSONL, and agents communicate through direct messages, team broadcasts, and a shared context store.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5ecd8e0f55cf6451263727dcc2012865189445fd8a7bf5ac96586463c8cca31b","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_47b43554f9089315148df656816f7be3e8dcbf98d6162e08c5ad7ec7e60b5eb7","slc_75836c599eb9953d43dc492806cf2a7a294f5b298fbcd05ba3355386cc81f04e","slc_7d54c53b4aa3513f221c3e008c27fa5ba74b9b7970e4233beb4fa0b7bdc782a3"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"The CLI is published as the npm package @oxgeneral/orch, installed globally, and launching `orch` in a project opens a TUI dashboard after auto-initialization.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_639e84802208e1b57113845f1f3b831ab7353ba48554e3009d850bdad05f0bdc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=relevance","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_65b02eec8205d6c6c5f1525e7cf8031256d98bd0ad7d563e57c6994e3d37da53","slc_6e0c731bf0d7c778c92c2706a949001a416c5959b0a10ea9f0463749e2d58f58","slc_fe7bd3d97fcdf38feecaecd87182d269496dc81450c0688431971caadc5b872e"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"ORCH targets solo founders and small teams running multiple AI coding/CLI agents on one project, positioning itself as open-source (MIT) orchestration where users pay only for their own AI API usage.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_73a2fa9a38b90e6f54419894110e30021ecd96cfae5bac23943d763303bf82e5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_53e7587bfb0bfca9c33054444f01c4bee8a6ad28c1a09458e4156f5a8a0a249c","slc_983a2a6a6a2d861b86fdb186a7a1ef8692b55aab821cc9655caff93dff3c0cb2"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"Eight adapters are documented: Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Pi, Cursor, Grok, Antigravity, and Shell, where the shell adapter wraps any terminal CLI tool as an agent.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7516dc2b3db2d8609a70e6c20dd1259b622fd18cf9f5c898f37ea6740ce0c709","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_62ea80c4d3eb0529da85a34650c89d6ca04e3f33a30ef48a00b0806d25b73d6a"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"The daemon enforces single-orchestrator-per-project via a lock file (.orchestry/orchestry.lock), shuts down gracefully on SIGINT/SIGTERM, logs heap usage each tick, and throttles idle-tick logging.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_81fca59ea3a29c8b3a5ac861dcd6d032cd4d76749a8650f0174e25496be49562","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_16ffacdb248fb4e85f5e1fabe1cb5e1753158165ff6267582162a62057bff966","slc_1c733d77ade770827b0edd65bad0e5491a5d0bcd52b16a0cf62b23cf13e30607","slc_5aa22e4d598f64a73f3ae0125b68556c5586fb7c3dde0d888529686a889afee5"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"Pre-built organization templates are provided (e.g. startup-mvp, pr-review-corp, migration-squad, security-dept, content-agency, data-lab, sales-machine, docs-team) deployable via `orch org deploy`, with export of custom setups.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_95b34a8fc44b365c6a4f30f774c90e4a0920f1eecc82f8a9fdfb9f711799b51e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f4c31a0757302d2ef1d4487241b34ee4ec017ba29179ac06fe5c00128f7e3dee","slc_f6abdb55a80b0361edc21f126ed6a4016ae0fab52a856ab706ad096d7682b2c4"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"The runtime requires Node.js >= 20 on macOS, Linux, or WSL2, and needs no database, cloud service, Docker, or GPU since LLMs are accessed via API.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9949c9c5f9fd94f16d5909b6e4d3269c1086caa0d7b11e2925b0499568a82229","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=skills-patterns","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_339f8f4aab152c3fccc8952a0d844042cf9c400037643c5c006fa877ae171c4a","slc_f5e05fa691b5890bce7977db3ba2c8dcb67ea4d74f639b60760af8b642799443"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"After installation, an `/orch` skill is reportedly available in Claude Code, translating natural-language requests into orch commands for agents, tasks, goals, and runs.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9956bb50131e6ed127f2eda66b23e5f9e86f16ab9649e0740bff89cada5036aa","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1e5ccc2a05ce81dfd30a1f3b9011b7280e7392cdf3c2cd4a9480fcdd8267af56","slc_7cbd391e9603a352eb146765684982d888fe2d4eddea28c74c5f7108a817164f"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"Each agent works in an isolated git worktree on its own branch, and code reaches main only after explicit user approval through a mandatory review step in the task state machine.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ca1122903fb4773dd73c69ec81c2d3eb6077f29fdb48bc2758aeda3ab49a3f82","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1f53bc59a9e4c69dd2a11d8162be6c7603a068a9498656e073a065e38d313721","slc_21ccdbc8ae421455b844474cfeaafabb995f386b89536450be0e528f402201eb","slc_451c24feec64aa0b127771c0ad501371d338656c359b017f72982b1e54c776ef"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"Serve mode emits one JSON line per event (e.g. agent:started, task:status_changed, orchestrator:tick) with configurable json/text format, optional log file, and a default 10000 ms tick interval.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_cab5a1fa178971ea023cffef36eb30af85c3a1faef14849d68af9daecd41baf5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4bc96f5ec6bc9b01ff373e20ede7b8bf892c3cde122ee598c6707c2979e8afe0","slc_578902d2c278605c1b7e3b9cdb93d3868694efd45c984b8274d73c93ace8d3d0"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"Tasks flow through a state machine (todo → in_progress → review → done) with validated transitions, and no code merges without approval.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","created_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d13e86e7b71a2d235b00d69607af451e7d611baabc9cec2863984070fc823c5a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"oxgeneral/orch@c066dc013e98 snapshot 63003115ba6c9391","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_f819496f3b72405e8a191593cc5c9a1ef58ed1ad27a8e11208708ec79a043f2a"],"source_ids":["src_1a8c9323c4b859c1958c10eabc7950f2"],"text":"The documented source layout includes domain (models, state machine), application (orchestrator engine, services, event bus), infrastructure (adapters, file storage, process management, LiquidJS templates, git worktree workspace), cli (Commander.js), and tui (Ink + React).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:29:04Z","updated_by_operation":"op_fe0baadd82904f6aac1cede4954d8849"}
